ttps://openalex.org/W2129524834", "https://openalex.org/W3125484365", "https://openalex.org/W2348399469", "https://openalex.org/W2113991325", "https://openalex.org/W1574015943", "https://openalex.org/W3124555074", "https://openalex.org/W1511413465", "https://openalex.org/W3121378619", "https://openalex.org/W1599449303", "https://openalex.org/W1972601484", "https://openalex.org/W1545731555", "https://openalex.org/W2101311377", "https://openalex.org/W3125644009", "https://openalex.org/W1978949361", "https://openalex.org/W2031274636", "https://openalex.org/W3123689064", "https://openalex.org/W1590283014", "https://openalex.org/W2137810944", "https://openalex.org/W4298863114", "https://openalex.org/W2032830535", "https://openalex.org/W2044392985", "https://openalex.org/W3122413074", "https://openalex.org/W1516775840", "https://openalex.org/W1981928741", "https://openalex.org/W1513281941", "https://openalex.org/W2542777094", "https://openalex.org/W1513709814"], "SJR": 25.102, "SJR_Normalized": 3.262011939745336, "abstract": "this paper develops a new approach to test for downward wage rigidity by examining transitory shocks to labor demand (i.e., rainfall) across 600 indian districts. nominal wages rise during positive shocks but do not fall during droughts. in addition, transitory positive shocks generate ratcheting: after they have dissipated, wages do not adjust back down. ratcheting reduces employment by 9 percent, indicating that rigidities distort employment levels. inflation, which is unaffected by local rainfall, enables downward real wage adjustments offering causal evidence for its labor market effects. surveys suggest that individuals believe nominal wage cuts are unfair and lead to effort reductions. (jel e24, e31, j23, j31, o15, o18, r23)", "publication_info": {"host_organization_name": "American Economic Association", "host_organization_lineage_names": [], "type": "journal"}, "classification_path": "Social Science > Social and Economic Geography > Human Geography > Migration Study"}, {"id": "https://openalex.org/W2883696333", "title": "from lonely to resilient through humanoid robots: building a new framework of resilience", "publication_date": "2018-07-19", "display_name": "From Lonely to Resilient through Humanoid Robots: Building a New Framework of Resilience", "authorships": [{"name": "Johan F. Hoorn", "position": "first", "institutions": ["Hong Kong Polytechnic University", "Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"], "countries": ["HK", "NL"], "is_corresponding": true}], "cited_by_count": 11, "referenced_works": ["https://openalex.org/W2113961844", "https://openalex.org/W1972847781", "https://openalex.org/W2031904986", "https://openalex.org/W2081155210", "https://openalex.org/W1979460778", "https://openalex.org/W2114836768", "https://openalex.org/W2065848138", "https://openalex.org/W2517763697", "https://openalex.org/W2062533360", "https://openalex.org/W2149194447", "https://openalex.org/W2024426706", "https://openalex.org/W2106849549", "https://openalex.org/W2140386575", "https://openalex.org/W2152524752", "https://openalex.org/W1984767015", "https://openalex.org/W2141846678", "https://openalex.org/W2061862181", "https://openalex.org/W2336265596", "https://openalex.org/W2154543439", "https://openalex.org/W2132164645", "https://openalex.org/W2145978062", "https://openalex.org/W2157257781", "https://openalex.org/W2471117963", "https://openalex.org/W2056380125", "https://openalex.org/W1516931150", "https://openalex.org/W2106968553", "https://openalex.org/W1483294286", "https://openalex.org/W2594825291", "https://openalex.org/W2061767427", "https://openalex.org/W2102561387", "https://openalex.org/W2336640934", "https://openalex.org/W591243655", "https://openalex.org/W2162417293", "https://openalex.org/W2467832538", "https://openalex.org/W2132050359", "https://openalex.org/W2051037982", "https://openalex.org/W4292854730", "https://openalex.org/W2014833927", "https://openalex.org/W2075220185", "https://openalex.org/W2055968533", "https://openalex.org/W2082985218", "https://openalex.org/W1980602541", "https://openalex.org/W2086849805", "https://openalex.org/W4251720919", "https://openalex.org/W2163467563", "https://openalex.org/W2029499893", "https://openalex.org/W2154406753", "https://openalex.org/W2138867401", "https://openalex.org/W1795505958", "https://openalex.org/W2165167678", "https://openalex.org/W2029526731"], "SJR": 0.508, "SJR_Normalized": 0.4107842695857643, "abstract": "this paper connects different theories and methods from the social sciences and applies them to human-humanoid robot interaction (hhri) to explain loneliness reduction and the build-up of resilience in older adults through social robots. it allows for user-related aspects such as age, social connectedness, gender role, personality, and need satisfaction as well as robot-related aspects, particularly coaching behaviors and communication styles. from these scientific considerations, solutions to design challenges are pinpointed, proposing novel interaction schemes that enhance the feeling of support and companionship. this paper also opens the way to conducting empirical research to examine hhri-related designs, measuring user experience in hhri, while suggesting applications in hhri in various settings, such as coaching and eldercare.", "publication_info": {"host_organization_name": "Hindawi Publishing Corporation", "host_organization_lineage_names": [], "type": "journal"}, "classification_path": "Social Science > Social and Economic Geography > Human Geography > Migration Study"}]